.\" Manpage for tadpole
.\" Generated by help2man or manually written
.TH TADPOLE 1 "November 2026" "Tadpole 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tadpole \- Native Linux desktop GUI for adb and fastboot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tadpole
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Tadpole
is a native Linux desktop application for managing Android devices via
.B adb
(Android Debug Bridge) and
.BR fastboot .
It provides a graphical interface for common device management tasks
without requiring a web browser or Electron.
.PP
The application features two main modes:
.TP
.B ADB Mode
For devices booted into Android (normal operation). Provides device overview,
app management, file browser, shell, logcat viewer, live screen view, and more.
.TP
.B Fastboot Mode
For devices in the bootloader. Provides variable reading, partition listing,
flashing with presets, bootloader unlock/lock, wipe, and reboot options.
.SH OPTIONS
.B tadpole
accepts no command-line options. All configuration is done through the GUI.
.SH USAGE
.TP
.B Starting
Run
.B tadpole
from your application menu or terminal.
.TP
.B Device Selection
Use the dropdown in the top bar to select a connected device.
The status pill shows the number of ready devices.
.TP
.B Mode Switch
Click "ADB" or "Fastboot" radio buttons in the top bar to switch modes.
.TP
.B Wireless ADB
In ADB mode, use "Connect\\(u2026" to connect via IP:port,
or "Pair\\(u2026" for WiFi pairing with a pairing code.
.TP
.B Drag and Drop
.TP
.RS
.IP \(bu
Drop
.B .apk
files in ADB mode to install them.
.IP \(bu
Drop
.B .img
or
.B .bin
files in Fastboot mode to prepare flashing.
.RE
.TP
.B Terminal Dock
The bottom terminal accepts raw
.B adb
or
.B fastboot
commands.
Use Up/Down arrows for history.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.tadpole/presets.json
Saved flash presets (partition, slot, image path, options).
.TP
.B ~/.tadpole/
Configuration directory (migrates from ~/.adb-studio/ if present).
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B System
Linux with Python 3.9+, Tkinter, adb, fastboot
.TP
.B Python Dependencies
tkinterdnd2 (drag & drop), sv-ttk (Sun Valley dark theme), Pillow (image scaling)
.SH INSTALLATION
Run the installer:
.RS
.PP
.B git clone https://github.com/FALLEN-arch/tadpole.git
.PP
.B cd tadpole && ./install.sh
.RE
.PP
This creates a virtual environment at
.BR ~/.local/share/tadpole/venv/ ,
installs Tadpole and dependencies, and adds a launcher to
.BR ~/.local/bin/tadpole .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Error (display server not available, etc.)
